Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 10:28:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [M154] ipcz: Correct transport trust and handle ownership for elevated peers

Original change's description:
> ipcz: Correct transport trust and handle ownership for elevated peers
>
> Invitation::Accept previously marked its transport toward the broker
> with is_peer_trusted=true unconditionally. When the acceptor is
> elevated, the broker is less privileged than the acceptor and should not
> be implicitly marked as trusted. Accept now sets is_peer_trusted based
> on whether the acceptor is elevated.
>
> Additionally, Transport::DecodeHandle now verifies that a broker peer is
> at least as privileged as the local endpoint (i.e., the local endpoint
> is not elevated relative to the broker) before accepting recipient-owned
> handles. Transport::SerializeObject is also updated to encode handles as
> kSender when the peer is elevated, allowing the more privileged peer to
> handle duplication.
>
